<%#
  ONE REAL SUBFOLDER of the project's folder, recursively — a section per subfolder, nested exactly
  as it sits on disk (stage 3, S3-1; "the folder is the truth" replaces the old role-derived
  grouping). A working tree renders here too, entered rather than stopped at
  (Maker::ProjectFolderListing#tree), with a link to its commit and history pages — a repository is
  a section now, and the old standalone Repositories group (_repo_group.html.erb) is gone. What is
  INSIDE that section changed on 2026-09-07: see "ALWAYS OPEN" below.

  @generated_ids IS FILTERED OUT HERE, AT EVERY LEVEL of the recursion, so a file with an addon
  origin renders ONCE, in the Generated group below, never inside the folder it happens to sit in
  (ProjectsController#show resolves @generated from @listing.node_ids, which already covers every
  depth of this tree).

  ALWAYS OPEN, WITH ONE EXCEPTION SINCE 2026-09-07. S2-2's "closed by default" rule belongs to the
  synthetic, cross-cutting Backups group alone (_attachment_group.html.erb, unchanged) — a REAL
  subfolder is not that, whatever a user happens to name it. A REPOSITORY is the second exception,
  at the user's request: it renders CLOSED, and what is inside it is the Finder-style browser
  (projects/_repo_browser) rather than tiles and nested sections. The reason is what a repo IS — a
  tree a maker NAVIGATES, whose files are read and edited on their own pages — where a plain
  subfolder is a handful of things to see at a glance. Unrolling a working tree into a section per
  directory buries the rest of the project's panel under someone's `src/`.

  THE COUNT IN THE SUMMARY IS THE WHOLE SUBTREE FOR A REPOSITORY AND THIS DIR'S OWN VISIBLE FILES
  FOR EVERY OTHER SECTION. A plain section shows exactly the tiles it renders and its subfolders
  carry their own counts beside it, so the direct-child number is the honest one there. A repository
  renders NO tiles at all since 2026-09-07 — the browser inside it holds every file at every depth —
  so the same number read "(3)" beside a repository holding 203 files. The recursive count is
  Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir#subtree_file_count, in memory over the tree the listing already
  built. Generated files are NOT subtracted from a repository's count, unlike a plain section's: the
  browser lists them like any other file, where a section genuinely does not render them (they are
  in the Generated group instead).

  A SECTION IS A NESTED FOLDER ONLY, SINCE 2026-09-08. A DEPTH-ONE subfolder of the project's
  folder is a PANEL now (projects/_folder_panel), so this partial is reached from that panel's
  `children` and from its own recursion — never from projects/_attachments, which no longer renders
  a section at all.

  Locals: dir (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir), view (one of Maker::Project::VIEWS) — the
  enclosing PANEL's view, passed down and passed on through the recursion. It was `@view`, one
  page-wide cookie, until the view became per panel (spec decision 6): an ivar cannot say which
  panel is asking.
%>
<% visible = dir.files.reject { |row| @generated_ids.include?(row.node_id) } %>
<% count = dir.repo? ? dir.subtree_file_count : visible.size %>
<section class="attachment-group file-tree-section">
  <%# `open` on everything but a repository — see the header. %>
  <details<%= " open" unless dir.repo? %>>
    <%# THE NAME AND THE COUNT STAY ON ONE SOURCE LINE, WITH ONE LITERAL SPACE BETWEEN THEM —
        _attachment_group.html.erb's summary does the same, and for the same reason: a conditional
        badge/link block on its own line leaves a newline-plus-indentation TEXT NODE behind even
        when it renders nothing, which breaks a `text: /name \(N\)/` substring match against the
        rendered summary (found by driving a real request, not by reading the template). %>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head"><%= dir.name %><% if dir.repo? %> <span class="badge">repo</span><% end %> <span class="muted">(<%= count %>)</span><% if dir.repo? %> <%= link_to "Commits", repo_commit_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn small" %> <%= link_to "History", repo_history_path(dir.node_id), class: "linkbtn small" %><% end %></summary>
    <%# THE CARD (stage 3, S3-2): README rendered, latest commit, current tag — at the top of the
        section, before its files. @repo_cards is keyed by node_id (ProjectsController#show) and
        holds one for every repo? Dir on the page, so a missing entry here would be a real bug, not
        a normal case — the `&&` guard is defensive rather than expected to ever fail. %>
    <% if dir.repo? %>
      <% if (card = @repo_cards[dir.node_id]) %>
        <%= render "projects/repo_card", card:, editable: false %>
      <% end %>
      <%# THE CARD STAYS ABOVE THE BROWSER and the browser replaces everything below it: no tiles,
          no rows, and NO nested file_tree_section collection. Recursing here as well would draw
          every subdirectory twice — once as a section and once as a column — and the section copy
          is the one that cannot answer "what is in src/?" without unrolling the whole tree. %>
      <%= render "projects/repo_browser", dir: %>
    <% else %>
      <% if visible.any? %>
        <% if view == "list" %>
          <%= render "file_rows", rows: visible %>
        <% else %>
          <div class="attachments-grid">
            <%= render partial: "file_tile", collection: visible, as: :row %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= render partial: "file_tree_section", collection: dir.children, as: :dir,
                 locals: { view: } %>
    <% end %>
  </details>
</section>
